  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi></math> be an odd natural number such that the variance of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#8230;</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>14</mn><mo>.</mo></math> Then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi></math> is equal to ________."
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "13",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Variance of n natural number is given by,</p><p>Variance<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>&#8721;</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo>-</mo><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mo>&#8721;</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>n</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>6</mn><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>-</mo><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mi>n</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p><p>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>6</mn></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mfenced><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mfenced><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mn>12</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>12</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>And it is given that Variance<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>14</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>12</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>14</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>168</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>13</mn></math></p>"
  }
